From: Opsero Electronic Design Inc. <support@opsero.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: axienet: exempt HSE MACs from the pcs-handle requirement

The XAXIENET_HSE mactype (UltraScale+ 100G CMAC / 40G-50G l_ethernet,
added by 0002-net-axienet-add-hse-cmac-l-ethernet-support.patch) has no
MDIO bus, PCS phy or external PHY: like MRMAC, link state is tracked by
polling RX alignment. The probe-time block that demands a pcs-handle or
phy-handle exempts every other PHY-less mactype but not HSE, so every
CMAC / l_ethernet port fails to probe:

  xilinx_axienet 80060000.l_ethernet: pcs-handle (preferred for
    1000BaseX/SGMII) or phy-handle required for external PHY
  xilinx_axienet 80060000.l_ethernet: probe with driver xilinx_axienet
    failed with error -22

Add the missing exemption. Found on first hardware boot of the
zcu106_hpc0 target (2x QSFP28 FMC, 2x 40GBASE-R4).
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
@@ -5808,6 +5808,7 @@
 	if (lp->axienet_config->mactype != XAXIENET_10G_25G &&
 	    lp->axienet_config->mactype != XAXIENET_1G_10G_25G &&
 	    lp->axienet_config->mactype != XAXIENET_MRMAC &&
+	    lp->axienet_config->mactype != XAXIENET_HSE &&
 	    lp->axienet_config->mactype != XAXIENET_DCMAC) {
 		np = of_parse_phandle(pdev->dev.of_node, "pcs-handle", 0);
 		if (!np) {
